{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter Prepares for Final Exams"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Accounting, What a Drag!"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 10}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations"}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.'"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Ask If/When People Are Free "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to spend time with someone, you ask them if or when they are free."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use these phrases to ask people if or when they are free:<br/><br/>Are you free on \u2026 ?<br/>How does (day) sound?<br/>When are you free to \u2026 ?<br/>What day are you free?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Are you free on Saturday? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "How does Sunday sound? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "When are you free to study for the exam?"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Modals Will, May, Might"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the modals <span class=\"italic\">may</span> and <span class=\"italic\">might</span> to show possibility. They have the same meaning.<br/>You use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span> to predict the future in a more certain way."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Modals go before a verb in the base form. The verb does not change."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I may take a futurology course next term. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I might be free if I finish the class project. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Technology will make our lives better. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We will have a world government."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "major"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in college or university, the subject of study of the majority of your courses"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm doing a major in Humanities."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about programs of study."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "minor"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in college or university, the subject of study of a few of your courses"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Accounting is only a minor for me."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "the Humanities"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "different subjects of study about people, such as history, philosophy, literature, religion, etc."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My courses are in the Humanities this term."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "literature"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the study of works of writing, like books, plays, poems, etc."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do you like your course in English literature?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "history"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the study of the past"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm very interested in world history."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "subject"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a topic of study in a school (different courses can be the same subject)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Humanities are subjects like literature and philosophy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "futurology"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the study of what might happen in the future"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I may take a futurology course next term."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob06aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "philosophy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the study of the knowledge and the way you think"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Philosophy is one of the courses in the Humanities."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob06aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "what a drag"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "it's a bad thing; it's inconvenient"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Too bad this course is compulsory. What a drag!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob06aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to predict"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to expect that something is going to happen in the future"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Futurology is the study of predicting the future. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le10ob06aud10"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le10ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write 4 - 5 sentences giving your opinion about predicting the future. Is it possible? Would you want to? Why or why not?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find 5 predictions for the future. Write them down."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your sentences to a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss the topic of futurology with your partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write my opinion."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I find 5 predictions for the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my sentences to a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss futurology with a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le10ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le10ob06re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le10ob06re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Another accounting class!  I really don't like this course.  <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jacob</span>:  I know what you mean.  Numbers and more numbers!  <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  Too bad this course is compulsory. What a drag! What other courses are you taking?", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le10ob06re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jacob</span>:  I'm doing a major in Humanities. Accounting is only a minor for me.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: What area of the Humanities?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jacob</span>:  It's subjects like history, literature and philosophy. Are you free on Saturday?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  I might be free. I have to finish the class project first.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jacob</span>:  The Humanities department is having a party on Saturday. Do you want to come?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:  I might go. Thanks!", "id": 2, "time": "13000", "image": "engenn5le10ob06re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jacob</span>:  I may take a futurology course next term.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Futurology? <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jacob</span>: Yeah, it's the study of predicting the future. We ask questi